{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: research note on agentic development practice. Head c81b168db1e008eb3397174b175e16eec3332d43, branch planner/agentic-practice-survey-20261026: one commit on Main a97c7425 (merge base equals Main). Review request 30d4cf83, checker promise a5483bbe, request a455fdba (planner promise 8c604866). Artifacts: the note (c0b7d53d) and the notes directory (8e3dc2c1).\n\nRead order: the note at the head in full; the review request's conditions; every cited source line and note line at a97c7425; the note's links; then the two scripts.\n\nOne gap blocks approval:\n1. Line 208 links to `2026-10-21-roles-flow-and-instances.md:275-278`. The link target includes the line suffix, so it names a file that does not exist and the link is broken. The line reference itself is correct: lines 275 to 278 of the roles note defer agent review to a later membership version and require that it refuse an agent whose controller controls an author. Fix: link to `2026-10-21-roles-flow-and-instances.md` and put \"lines 275-278\" in the text. check-doc-links did not catch it because it does not count links in notes/. The other eight relative links resolve at the head.\n\nTwo small fixes worth making in the same recut (not blocking):\n2. Line 202 quotes the landing policy as \"large, own design\". Its order table (line 177) says \"large (own design)\". Either quote it exactly or remove the quotation marks.\n3. Line 180 puts \"CI workflow files always need one person\" in quotation marks as \"the field's\". Section 2 does not quote it, and the text names no source for it. The Claude Code team's article supports the substance: sensitive paths always need a person, and CI workflows are among the code people review. Name that article as the source, or paraphrase without quotation marks.\n\nConditions met:\n- Scope: the delta against Main is the one new file, 313 lines and 18,741 bytes. git diff --check is clean.\n- Source citations, read at a97c7425:\n  - change.t